**The read: Enneagram Type 1 (1w2), confidence medium-high.**

The thesis is that Clark's driver is a private accounting of hours, not the scoreboard. The tiebreaker against Type 3 is her own words in a 2026 ESPN sit-down, where she was handed the flattering answer and refused it: *"I don't think it's like an obsession with winning. I think that comes because you're obsessed with all the time you put in."* A Three protects the visible result; Clark disclaimed it, and at Iowa she burned enough room-management capital holding teammates to her standard that Lisa Bluder ejected her from practice.

The hook is the six. Asked in 2026 to rate herself out of ten, she answered instantly and low, months before the only 40-point/10-assist game in WNBA history.

